! Constructions from the PDF (Chicago 5A, new construction, 90.1-2004): wall U = 0.084 Btu/h-ft2-F (Table 20, steel frame wall: Table 18 gives steel frame for the Secondary School and the xlsx names steel-framed walls), roof U = 0.063 (Table 19, insulation entirely above deck: Table 17). The layer resistance is 1/U minus the surface films.
  Material:NoMass,
    ExteriorWallLayer,            !- Name  Source: NREL PDF Table 20, p.36: steel frame wall U = 0.084 Btu/h-ft2-F; R = 1/U - films (0.1496 m2-K/W: interior 0.1197 + exterior 0.0299, 90.1-2004) = 1.9469 m2-K/W.
    MediumRough,                  !- Roughness
    1.9469;                       !- Thermal Resistance {m2-K/W}

  Construction,
    ExteriorWall,                 !- Name
    ExteriorWallLayer;            !- Outside Layer

  Material:NoMass,
    RoofLayer,                    !- Name  Source: NREL PDF Table 19, p.36: roof U = 0.063 Btu/h-ft2-F; R = 1/U - films (0.1373 m2-K/W: interior 0.1074 + exterior 0.0299, 90.1-2004) = 2.6581 m2-K/W.
    MediumRough,                  !- Roughness
    2.6581;                       !- Thermal Resistance {m2-K/W}

  Construction,
    Roof,                         !- Name
    RoofLayer;                    !- Outside Layer

  Material:NoMass,
    GenericLayer,                 !- Name  Not in the documents: EnergyPlus needs a construction for the interior walls, floors and ceilings; the resistance 0.2 m2-K/W is assumed.
    MediumRough,                  !- Roughness
    0.2;                          !- Thermal Resistance {m2-K/W}, round value; no thermal mass

  Construction,
    GenericSurface,               !- Name
    GenericLayer;                 !- Outside Layer

  WindowMaterial:SimpleGlazingSystem,
    Glazing,                      !- Name
    3.2366,                       !- U-Factor {W/m2-K}  Source: NREL PDF Table 24, p.38: window overall U = 0.57 Btu/h-ft2-F = 3.2366 W/m2-K.
    0.39;                         !- Solar Heat Gain Coefficient  Source: NREL PDF Table 25, p.39: SHGC = 0.39.

  Construction,
    Window,                       !- Name
    Glazing;                      !- Outside Layer

! Slab on grade: F-factor method; the PDF (Table 22, p.37) gives no insulation required (NR); F = 1.26363 W/m-K is the 90.1-2004 value of an uninsulated slab. Area and perimeter are computed from the polygons.
  Construction:FfactorGroundFloor,
    Corner_Class_1_Pod_1_ZN_1_FLR_1_Floor_Ffactor,!- Name
    1.26363,                      !- F-Factor {W/m-K}
    99.0,                         !- Area {m2}  Derived from: the area of the floor polygon of the surface Corner_Class_1_Pod_1_ZN_1_FLR_1_Floor (99 m2 = 1065.627 ft2 from the vertex coordinates).
    20.0;                         !- PerimeterExposed {m}  Derived from: the sum of the bottom edges of the 2 exterior walls that stand on the floor of the zone (Corner_Class_1_Pod_1_ZN_1_FLR_1_Wall_1, Corner_Class_1_Pod_1_ZN_1_FLR_1_Wall_4): 11 + 9 = 20 m.

